    <heading level="1">Everyday Math</heading>
    <exercise number="199" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Making a fence Jovani has a fence around the rectangular garden in his backyard. The perimeter of the fence is $$150$$ feet. The length is $$15$$ feet more than the width. Find the width, $$w,$$ by solving the equation $${150 = 2{({w + 15})} + 2w}.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>30 feet</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="200" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Concert tickets At a school concert, the total value of tickets sold was $$\text{\$1,506.}$$ Student tickets sold for $$\text{\$6}$$ and adult tickets sold for $$\text{\$9.}$$ The number of adult tickets sold was $$5$$ less than $$3$$ times the number of student tickets. Find the number of student tickets sold, $$s,$$ by solving the equation $${6s + 9{({3s - 5})} = 1506}.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="201" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Coins Rhonda has $$\text{\$1.90}$$ in nickels and dimes. The number of dimes is one less than twice the number of nickels. Find the number of nickels, $$n,$$ by solving the equation $${0.05n + 0.10(2n - 1) = 1.90}.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>8 nickels</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="202" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Fencing Micah has $$74$$ feet of fencing to make a rectangular dog pen in his yard. He wants the length to be $$25$$ feet more than the width. Find the length, $$L,$$ by solving the equation $${2L + 2(L - 25) = 74}.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
